column4:
INT_MIN / -1 works fine for me on amd64 with gcc 4.9. It produces INT_MIN, just as you would expect. INT_MIN * -1 is also INT_MIN.<p><pre><code>  #include <limits.h>
  #include <stdio.h>

  void main(void) {
          int x = INT_MIN;
          printf(&quot;INT_MIN = %d\n&quot;, x);
          printf(&quot;INT_MIN * -1 = %d\n&quot;, x * -1);
          printf(&quot;INT_MIN / -1 = %d\n&quot;, x / -1);
  }</code></pre>
